    sha256: 90b6c5ec739d2366936d67d78cd5a6f857b764b92000200f4a44ac956c88b3ac
  body: "# Assessment period for income other than self-employment\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe
    captured general-income guidance requires the claim date, benefit-week start, due date, date treated
    as paid and the relevant payment period or prescribed alternative before determining the period of
    assessment.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 25031 expressly excludes self-employment from these
    timing rules. Termination payments, overlapping earnings, part weeks and certain benefit payments
    have further provisions. This is an evidence checklist from the source, not a calendar or payment
    calculator; it is not a Pension Credit assessment-period definition.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 25031, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch25`: PDF SHA-256 `39edc3ed8ee9c875eb68ce4cd4148194b23dbd23bb6444883a2f2cae90a75337`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `db488637a179cc93910c4e243381b5c961d6959ce72cd1d34aff14e403517e73`.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch27`:
    PDF SHA-256 `90b6c5ec739d2366936d67d78cd5a6f857b764b92000200f4a44ac956c88b3ac`; extracted pages SHA-256
    `7f84279f4a44373405ce06d32bf1c927a9f25dda507895b1540e6bb8b1b5185a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-income-payment-dates
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passage explicitly lists the due date and the date treated as paid as separate
      inputs.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch25/0007
      quote: "25031   To determine the period over which any income other than income from self-\n   \
        \     employment is taken into account the DM needs to establish\n\n        1.    the date of
        claim\n\n        2.    the first day of the claimant's benefit week (see DMG 25052 - 25054)\n\n\
        \        3.    the date on which the income is due to be paid (see DMG 25034 et seq)\n\n     \
        \   4.    the date on which the income is treated as paid (see DMG 25043 et seq) and\n\n     \
        \   5.    either1\n\n              5.1   the period for which the payment is made or\n\n     \
        \         5.2   the amount of\n\n                    5.2.a    JSA or IS that would be payable
        without the income and\n\n                    5.2.b    any disregard the DM would normally make
        on the weekly\n                             amount of the income.\n\n        See DMG Chapter 26
        on earnings disregards and DMG Chapter 28 on other\n        income with partial disregards.\n\n\
        \        Note 1: If the income is a payment of earnings when employment ends see DMG"
      locator: DMG 25031
  - target: term/jsais-self-employed-assessment-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The general-income passage excludes self-employment; chapter 27 instead uses receipts
      and expenses during its own assessment period. This records a scope distinction rather than
      equivalence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch25/0007
      quote: "25031   To determine the period over which any income other than income from self-\n   \
        \     employment is taken into account the DM needs to establish\n\n        1.    the date of
        claim\n\n        2.    the first day of the claimant's benefit week (see DMG 25052 - 25054)\n\n\
        \        3.    the date on which the income is due to be paid (see DMG 25034 et seq)\n\n     \
        \   4.    the date on which the income is treated as paid (see DMG 25043 et seq) and\n\n     \
        \   5.    either1\n\n              5.1   the period for which the payment is made or\n\n     \
        \         5.2   the amount of\n\n                    5.2.a    JSA or IS that would be payable
        without the income and\n\n                    5.2.b    any disregard the DM would normally make
        on the weekly\n                             amount of the income.\n\n        See DMG Chapter 26
        on earnings disregards and DMG Chapter 28 on other\n        income with partial disregards.\n\n\
        \        Note 1: If the income is a payment of earnings when employment ends see DMG"
      locator: DMG 25031
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0014
      quote: "27051 The normal weekly earnings of a S/E earner should be calculated by using the\n\n\n\
        1. gross receipts (see DMG 27125) and\n\n\n2. expenses paid out (see DMG 27190)\n\n\nduring the
        assessment period. Different rules apply for royalties, copyright payments and Public Lending\n\
        Rights payments."
      locator: DMG 27051
